WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:02.270
- If you've already heard
of the Nürburgring,

00:00:02.270 --> 00:00:04.000
then by all means, enjoy this video.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:05.730
We've got an interview behind the scenes,

00:00:05.730 --> 00:00:07.500
some footage of the place,

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:11.360
but also we have me trying
to explain the basics of it

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:14.960
while being driven round the
Nordschleife, the North Loop

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:17.810
by a professional driver.
Thank you, Andy.

00:00:17.810 --> 00:00:19.763
But if you haven't heard
of the Nürburgring,

00:00:19.763 --> 00:00:22.910
then it may surprise you
that one of the greatest,

00:00:22.910 --> 00:00:25.640
most demanding racetracks in the world

00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:28.340
is also just a public toll road.

00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:31.470
And if you want, you can
just turn up and drive it.

00:00:33.190 --> 00:00:37.888
All right, I'm going to
regret this. Let's do it.

00:00:37.888 --> 00:00:40.200
- All right. Let's do it.

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:42.860
- There were always these
three big components.

00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:45.970
So one, that the Nordschleife
is open for the public.

00:00:45.970 --> 00:00:47.610
Then there's car testing.

00:00:47.610 --> 00:00:49.730
The big manufacturers
are still testing many,

00:00:49.730 --> 00:00:52.070
many weeks every year
here on the Nordschleife,

00:00:52.070 --> 00:00:54.310
the new components, the new cars.

00:00:54.310 --> 00:00:56.230
And of course, there's also racing.

00:00:56.230 --> 00:00:58.150
- Normal traffic rules apply here.

00:00:58.150 --> 00:01:01.530
You have to drive on the right,
you have to overtake on the left.

00:01:01.530 --> 00:01:04.460
But on most of the track,
there is no speed limit.

00:01:04.460 --> 00:01:08.000
And that's because Germany
has no national speed limit.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:10.090
There are thousands of
kilometres of autobahn out there

00:01:10.090 --> 00:01:13.410
where you can drive as
fast as you safely can.

00:01:13.410 --> 00:01:15.240
As long as you're in
control of your vehicle,

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:16.073
speed doesn't matter.

00:01:16.073 --> 00:01:20.070
So legally, this is just
a one way toll road.

00:01:20.070 --> 00:01:22.820
You go to the barrier, you pay your €25,

00:01:22.820 --> 00:01:25.400
you go through this bit
with the cones and the speed limit,

00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:28.073
and then you are on the Ring.

00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:31.066
Oh, yes!

00:01:31.066 --> 00:01:32.500
[Tom laughs]

00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:36.040
- 20.8 kilometres.
The Nürburgring Nordschleife is the

00:01:36.040 --> 00:01:38.370
longest permanent racetrack in the world.

00:01:38.370 --> 00:01:42.040
It's in the most popular and most
famous racetracks in the world,

00:01:42.040 --> 00:01:45.270
comparable to Indianapolis,
to Monaco, to Daytona.

00:01:45.270 --> 00:01:47.968
- But there are lots of safety rules,
and the team here--

00:01:47.968 --> 00:01:49.280
--oh my God--

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:50.760
--the team here asked me to make it clear

00:01:50.760 --> 00:01:52.730
that racing on the Ring on days like this

00:01:52.730 --> 00:01:53.940
is not allowed.

00:01:53.940 --> 00:01:56.960
And you'll see the cars ahead,
when we're on the straights,

00:01:56.960 --> 00:01:59.510
they indicate right,
they get out of the way,

00:01:59.510 --> 00:02:02.530
because legally on the autobahn,
that's what you have to do.

00:02:02.530 --> 00:02:06.330
Lap timers and dashcams
are forbidden.

00:02:06.330 --> 00:02:08.160
I mean, we've got special
permission for these cameras... 

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:09.106
...my...

00:02:09.106 --> 00:02:10.371
[strained noise]

00:02:11.130 --> 00:02:11.963
We've got special permission,

00:02:11.963 --> 00:02:14.900
but none of these cars should
have dashcams or timers

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:17.333
because it is just too dangerous...

00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:23.220
...it is too dangerous to
have a clock ticking

00:02:23.220 --> 00:02:25.640
either on your dashboard
or in your head.

00:02:25.640 --> 00:02:28.490
The track is unforgiving.

00:02:28.490 --> 00:02:32.200
If you come off here, you're
not rolling onto grass.

00:02:32.200 --> 00:02:33.490
You're not rolling onto gravel.

00:02:33.490 --> 00:02:36.310
You are hitting a barrier, or worse,

00:02:36.310 --> 00:02:38.560
you're hitting- Oh, that was a drop!

00:02:38.560 --> 00:02:39.620
You're hitting someone else.

00:02:39.620 --> 00:02:42.290
The track-- oh!--
It has jumps.

00:02:42.290 --> 00:02:45.410
It has sections where you will--
oh my God--

00:02:45.410 --> 00:02:49.340
get what roller coaster
fans would call air time.

00:02:49.340 --> 00:02:52.660
Not quite ejector time, but air time.

00:02:52.660 --> 00:02:54.280
- Everyone is able to drive.

00:02:54.280 --> 00:02:59.500
Of course, everyone who is sticking
to the rules of our driving standards.

00:02:59.500 --> 00:03:02.310
And of course, which
cars finally fit to us,

00:03:02.310 --> 00:03:05.060
that's 2.8 tonnes, is the max.

00:03:05.060 --> 00:03:06.870
People driving here round
with their Porsche,

00:03:06.870 --> 00:03:10.660
but you've also got a family driving
in their van here round.

00:03:10.660 --> 00:03:12.820
- There is a story that if you crash,

00:03:12.820 --> 00:03:16.650
then the Nürburgring team will present you
with a bill for damage.

00:03:16.650 --> 00:03:18.680
For every half-hour the
safety car had to be out here,

00:03:18.680 --> 00:03:22.430
for every half-hour that
they had to repair the track,

00:03:22.430 --> 00:03:25.690
for every metre of crash barrier
that you have damaged.

00:03:25.690 --> 00:03:27.969
That story is absolutely, 100%...

00:03:27.969 --> 00:03:32.150
true. If you are conscious, you
will be delivered a bill,

00:03:32.150 --> 00:03:34.460
but it turns out that's also
true in most of the world.

00:03:34.460 --> 00:03:36.930
If you crash on a British road,

00:03:36.930 --> 00:03:39.730
then the local highways
authority will send out a bill.

00:03:39.730 --> 00:03:43.231
It's just that it'll go to your
insurance company, not to you.

00:03:43.231 --> 00:03:44.603
Oh, g-forces!

00:03:48.020 --> 00:03:53.020
But insurance, other than very,
very good German insurance,

00:03:53.310 --> 00:03:54.600
it won't cover you for the Ring.

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:58.840
Nearly every insurance company,
particularly those outside Germany

00:03:58.840 --> 00:04:03.140
has a clause in there that
specifically excludes driving here,

00:04:03.140 --> 00:04:05.493
even if you are just a tourist.

00:04:06.620 --> 00:04:10.360
- In case of a heavier accident,
then the track gets closed.

00:04:10.360 --> 00:04:14.540
In case of a normal incident
like a technical breakdown,

00:04:14.540 --> 00:04:17.710
then it might be that it's
just getting under yellow.

00:04:17.710 --> 00:04:19.510
First of all, we've got marshals around

00:04:19.510 --> 00:04:23.390
and permanent contact to our operators
here in the entrance.

00:04:23.390 --> 00:04:25.470
We've got an emergency number

00:04:25.470 --> 00:04:29.320
and what we are now having
also from 2021 on

00:04:29.320 --> 00:04:34.150
is that we are starting to provide the
Nordschleife with camera operators.

00:04:34.150 --> 00:04:35.360
- So that is a speed limit.

00:04:35.360 --> 00:04:38.150
We have just hit a speed
limit for this corner

00:04:38.150 --> 00:04:39.283
and I can see why.

00:04:43.250 --> 00:04:46.020
And then as soon as you pass this line?

00:04:46.020 --> 00:04:47.253
Yep! Off we go.

00:04:48.090 --> 00:04:48.923
- Two years ago,

00:04:48.923 --> 00:04:52.960
we had statistics that
every 15,000 kilometres,

00:04:52.960 --> 00:04:55.520
an incident is happening
on the Nürburgring.

00:04:55.520 --> 00:04:58.850
But an incident might also
be a car losing fluid,

00:04:58.850 --> 00:05:02.390
some technical issues, but
also of course, an accident.

00:05:02.390 --> 00:05:04.340
I think the biggest difference is

00:05:04.340 --> 00:05:07.050
when you've got an
accident on a normal road,

00:05:07.050 --> 00:05:09.920
it takes quite a time until
you've got some emergency,

00:05:09.920 --> 00:05:13.700
here, we've got around
60 people of track safety

00:05:13.700 --> 00:05:16.943
and track operators making
this track as safe as possible.

00:05:19.129 --> 00:05:20.443
- There's a banked turn?

00:05:22.487 --> 00:05:23.330
[Tom laughs]

00:05:23.330 --> 00:05:26.210
- There isn't another racetrack
like the Nordschleife.

00:05:26.210 --> 00:05:28.260
It just built into the landscape.

00:05:28.260 --> 00:05:32.120
Normally, landscapes are
constructed for racetracks.

00:05:32.120 --> 00:05:33.690
- Out of the way!

00:05:33.690 --> 00:05:37.210
- It is so challenging because it's
so narrow and it's so long.

00:05:37.210 --> 00:05:40.070
The barriers are so close to the racetrack

00:05:40.070 --> 00:05:42.850
and yeah, I guess that's
what makes it challenging,

00:05:42.850 --> 00:05:44.730
but what also the drivers love.

00:05:44.730 --> 00:05:46.871
- Little jump. 3, 2, 1, here.

00:05:46.871 --> 00:05:47.704
- Oh, boy!

00:05:49.556 --> 00:05:51.597
[Tom laughs]

00:05:51.597 --> 00:05:53.950
And across the line!

00:05:53.950 --> 00:05:54.783
Wow!

00:05:58.820 --> 00:06:00.080
- I hope you enjoyed it.

00:06:00.080 --> 00:06:01.730
Oh, yes!

00:06:01.730 --> 00:06:03.910
That was incredible!

00:06:03.910 --> 00:06:06.599
I have never done
anything like that before.

00:06:06.599 --> 00:06:10.130
I like racing now! I like racetracks.

00:06:10.130 --> 00:06:10.963
Wow.

00:06:12.800 --> 00:06:15.860
Every time, every time I've
done something like this,

00:06:15.860 --> 00:06:17.510
I've gone in thinking
I'm going to hate it.

00:06:17.510 --> 00:06:19.130
I've gone in thinking
it's going to be terrible,

00:06:19.130 --> 00:06:20.780
I'm going to be terrified.

00:06:20.780 --> 00:06:22.853
And every time I've loved it.

00:06:24.710 --> 00:06:25.573
Yes!

00:06:26.870 --> 00:06:29.490
I loved every second of that.

00:06:29.490 --> 00:06:31.010
I want to do that again.

00:06:31.010 --> 00:06:32.950
Thank you so much to Andy, my driver.

00:06:32.950 --> 00:06:36.657
Thank you so much to all the
team here at the Nürburgring.

00:06:37.870 --> 00:06:39.339
Oh, that's wonderful!

